  - name: HAProxy Backend Down
    detail: checks for a non-zero connection failure rate from HAProxy to backend servers.
    calendar: OfficeHours
    fluxfile: flux/haproxy_downtime_rate.flux
    severity: 1
    threshold: 0.0
    comparison: gt
    tags: 
      - host
      - _field
      - _measurement
      - proxy
      - sv
    interval: 120 
    target: xapi
    action: | 
              This alert indicates that the load-balancer cannot establish a connection to the backends on WLS servers. 
              Connect to any affected Weblogic server and Weblogic console. Manually check that the applications are up and look at 
              logs for any errors that would indicate that one or more products are non-operational.  
              Look for excessive load on Azure Portal dashboards (CPU). This alert may be sent during simple high load but 
              most llkely a WLS Node has a fault and will need to be restarted.
